A||||4||Alex2004||How do I install a 3rd brake light on an 84 SE?||||5||
Z||000000||Alex2004||12-25-2000||06:03 PM||||I have an 84 SE, and i have a 3rd brake light from an 86 GT. How would i install it? And where would i splice the wires? let me know if you know how. Thanks<BR>Alex...<P>             <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||82-T/A||12-26-2000||08:26 AM||||You could probably splice it into the existing brake lights, and run a wire through the firewall, up through the A-pillar, through the roof over the headliner, and into the back there. I don't think it's got the mounting brackets however, so your going to have to think of some way to fashion it yourself.. maybe JB Weld?<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-26-2000||10:50 AM||||It would seem to me that you will have to run a new wire from the pedal brake light switch to the 3rd brake light. You don't want to tie in with the directional signal circuit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||12-26-2000||10:50 PM||||Seems like I've answered this sort of question before  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Phil's correct.  You want to tap into the brake switch - the blue wire.<P>If you tapped into the brake/DS lamps at the back of the car, you'd soon get tired of the blinkin' thing, well... blinking.  Besides, when you tap into the brake pedal switch, all the new wiring can stay inside the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||Alex2004||12-26-2000||11:04 PM||||I went outside and looked at the brake switch. There are 4 wires!?! orange, white, light purple, & pink w/ black stripe. So, what should i do? I tapped into the purple to see but nothing happened, and i tested the test light before i did that also. So...any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||4
